THE DIFF UNDER TEST (one executable line)
  -  if (a0 >= 1)
  +  if ((int64_t)a0 >= 1 && (int64_t)a0 <= 3)
        cpu->invalidate_translation_caches(cpu, a1, INVALIDATE_VADDR);
     else
        cpu->invalidate_translation_caches(cpu, 0, INVALIDATE_ALL);

SIBLING PARITY  -- compare the two arms' observable channels
  arm S (selective, INVALIDATE_VADDR, addr=a1): flushes ONLY the entry whose
        vaddr_page matches a1's page.  Observable: an unrelated warmed page keeps
        its stale translation.
  arm C (conservative, INVALIDATE_ALL, addr=0): flushes every valid entry.
        Observable: an unrelated warmed page loses its translation and re-walks.

  ASYMMETRY 1, and it is the reason these rows exist: the SHIPPED 7-row witness has
  NO row that can tell arm S from arm C.  Every one of its rows observes only the
  TARGET page, and the target is flushed by both arms.  Rows owed: at least one row
  observing a NON-target page, per side of each bound.

  ASYMMETRY 2, and it is a row the 3-row design does not contain.
  The fix's guard is a TWO-SIDED window [1,3].  Enumerating the four sides:
        lower bound, accept side (a0=1, must be arm S)   -> row "bnd lo"    PLANNED
        lower bound, reject side (a0=0, must be arm C)   -> NO ROW PLANNED  <-- GAP
        upper bound, accept side (a0=3, must be arm S)   -> row "bnd hi"    PLANNED
        upper bound, reject side (a0=4, must be arm C)   -> row "bnd out"   PLANNED
  Three of the four sides are covered.  The missing one admits the clause-(d) mutant
  `>= 1' -> `>= 0' (a bound RELAXED -- squarely inside the (d) enumeration), which is
  PREDICTED to be a CLEAN SWEEP of the 10-row detector: a0=0 is the only selector
  whose arm it changes, and no row drives a0=0.
  DISPOSITION: build it (M_D) and MEASURE.  If it sweeps, that is an L2 floor breach,
  and the row is added and re-measured IN-ROUND rather than filed.
  This instantiates the near/far-bound lesson one level down: an accept row pins the
  bound it SITS ON, so a window needs a row on each side of each bound.  Counting
  rows is not the same as counting sides.

CLAIM -> ROW  (added comment sentences asserting an observable consequence)
  "A guest TBIA/TBIAP therefore flushed ONE page and left every other cached
   translation live."
      -> rows "tbia obs", "tbiap obs" (shipped) observe the TARGET page only.  The
         "left every other cached translation live" half was rowed by NOTHING until
         these accept rows; "bnd lo"/"bnd hi" are what observe an OTHER page.
  "1, 2 and 3 are the only selective ops ... 0 and 4.. are undefined and fall to the
   conservative arm with the negatives."
      -> a0=1 "bnd lo"; a0=2 "pos obs" (shipped, but see the vacuity note below --
         it cannot see which arm ran); a0=3 "bnd hi"; a0=4 "bnd out";
         a0=0 OWED (asymmetry 2); a0=-1/-2 "tbiap obs"/"tbia obs".
  "Over-invalidation cannot serve a stale translation; under-invalidation can."
      -> N/A with reason: a statement about the SAFETY ORDERING of the two arms, not
         about an observable of this build.  No row owed.
  "both map to INVALIDATE_ALL -- EXACT for -2 and CONSERVATIVE for -1"
      -> NO ROW POSSIBLE, stated rather than glossed: this model's translation cache
         carries no ASM/ASN metadata, so -1 and -2 are INDISTINGUISHABLE by any probe
         against this model.  A row claiming to separate them would be vacuous by
         construction.
  "NO ANNOUNCE, deliberately"
      -> an absence claim; discharged by reading the hunk (no debugmsg/fatal added),
         not by a row.  N/A with reason recorded.

GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD
  guard predicate reads:  a0            (only)
  guarded body reads:     a1, INVALIDATE_VADDR      (arm S)
                          literal 0, INVALIDATE_ALL (arm C)
  THEY DIFFER: the guard reads a0 and the body reads a1.  Both are guest registers
  written by the guest immediately before CALL_PAL, at independent sites, so a
  DISAGREEING state (a0 inside [1,3] while a1 names an unexpected page, a1=0
  included) is freely reachable.
  Body-induced partition of a1: NONE -- the body does not TEST a1, it passes it as an
  argument.  Under the joint-cell rule, a value the body never tests as a case is
  clause-(e) DISCLOSURE, not floor.
  DISCLOSED, and measured rather than argued: the conjunct `&& a1 != 0' is predicted
  to escape, because every row drives a1=0x6000 on the selective arm, and the two
  negative-selector rows that do set a1=0 take arm C, where a1 is ignored.  Built as
  M_E.  The direction of the resulting error is CONSERVATIVE (tbi(1,0) would
  over-invalidate), so it is coverage debt rather than a live defect -- recorded
  either way.

CHANNEL  -- per row: the mutant it kills, and the observable that differs under it
  row        mutant killed                      observable that differs under it
  ---------  ---------------------------------  -----------------------------------
  bnd lo     `>= 1' -> `>= 2'                   obs Y (VA 0x4000): VAL_C -> VAL_D
                                                (a0=1 wrongly takes arm C, Y flushed)
  bnd hi     `<= 3' -> `<= 2'                   obs Y: VAL_C -> VAL_D
                                                (a0=3 wrongly takes arm C, Y flushed)
  bnd out    `<= 3' -> `<= 4'                   obs Y: VAL_D -> VAL_C
                                                (a0=4 wrongly takes arm S, Y spared)
  bnd zero   `>= 1' -> `>= 0'                   obs Y: VAL_D -> VAL_C
             [ROW OWED -- asymmetry 2]          (a0=0 wrongly takes arm S, Y spared)

  Each named channel CAN vary under its named mutant, because obs Y is the one cell
  the two arms disagree about.  obs X is a CONTROL: it is VAL_F under BOTH arms by
  construction, so no row rests on it varying, and it is deliberately not the
  discriminator.  It is carried in the row so that a session which silently failed to
  run, or failed to invalidate the target at all, cannot present as green.

  VACUITY NOTE ON A SHIPPED ROW: "pos obs" (a0=2) names no mutant it can kill.  Its
  channel -- the target page's own value -- does not vary between the arms, so it
  cannot see any bound edit.  It is a liveness/positive control, not a bound row,
  which is precisely why sessions 4-6 are owed.  Recorded here rather than silently
  relied on.

